<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">From attribute to obligation, in four steps. <span>An attribute on the record, the rule it triggers, the work it creates, and the record it feeds.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="bento">
      <li class="bento-card bento-card--full">
        <h3 class="h4">A diesel tank, under SPCC</h3>
        <ol class="chain">
          <li><span class="chain-step">Attribute</span>300 bbl of diesel (12,600 gallons) in a single-wall tank.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Rule</span>SPCC, 40 CFR 112: over 1,320 gallons of aboveground oil storage. Containment for the largest tank plus freeboard.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Work</span>Berm and tank inspections on the compliance schedule. A leak opens a corrective action.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Record</span>The SPCC plan stays current from the inspection record, not from a binder.</li>
        </ol>
        <a class="text-action" href="/spcc">See SPCC</a>
      </li>
      <li class="bento-card bento-card--full">
        <h3 class="h4">Fuel use, into the inventories</h3>
        <ol class="chain">
          <li><span class="chain-step">Attribute</span>A fuel use tag in mcf a month, pulled in from telemetry.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Rule</span>GHG reporting under 40 CFR 98, and the state emission inventory.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Work</span>Calculation groups compute emissions as each reading arrives, with our methods or yours.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Record</span>Monthly CO2 in metric tons, with the readings, method, and factor version behind it.</li>
        </ol>
        <a class="text-action" href="/platform/emissions">See emissions</a>
      </li>
      <li class="bento-card bento-card--full">
        <h3 class="h4">Components, into an LDAR program</h3>
        <ol class="chain">
          <li><span class="chain-step">Attribute</span>Components and their service type, rolled up from component to plant.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Rule</span>NSPS OOOOb or the state program, applied by facility type and state.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Work</span>Survey rounds dispatched by rule. Repair, retest, and verification on each finding.</li>
          <li><span class="chain-step">Record</span>Open days feed the fugitive emission record for subpart W.</li>
        </ol>
        <a class="text-action" href="/ldar">See LDAR</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">When a rule changes, you see what it touches. <span>Every asset, inspection, and form maps to the citation it satisfies, so a change reads across the fleet, not asset by asset.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-runs">
      <li><h3>Which assets does this rule govern?</h3><p>Each citation lists the assets mapped to it, across every site.</p></li>
      <li><h3>What work did it create?</h3><p>Tasks are created against the compliance schedule, maintenance programs, and inspections, and sit on the asset.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Which reports does this reading feed?</h3><p>Calculation lineage keeps the source readings behind every reported figure.</p></li>
      <li><h3>What was the limit that day?</h3><p>Point-in-time requirements: the limit in force on the date the work was done.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

