<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2>What compliance leads ask about the record.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Does this replace the Compliance, LDAR, and SPCC modules?</summary>
        <div><p>No. Those modules run the programs. This is the asset side: the attributes and readings every program reads from.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can we use our own emission calculation methods?</summary>
        <div><p>Yes. Use our calculation methodologies or build your own. The method and factor version are recorded with each result.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which rules can be mapped to an asset?</summary>
        <div><p>Federal, state, and permit-specific: 40 CFR 98, 40 CFR 112, NSPS and NESHAP subparts, state inventories, and your Title V conditions.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How does an auditor trace a reported figure?</summary>
        <div><p>From the figure to its calculation, then to the readings, method, and factor version behind it, and on to the asset that produced them.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

